    <td style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">All
    Other Compensation for fiscal year 2026 consisted of Company contributions for medical insurance and 401(k) matching contributions
    as follows: Nicholas D. Gerber&#8212;medical insurance $43,198; 401(k) matching contribution $14,000; total $57,198; David W. Neibert&#8212;medical
    insurance $44,869; 401(k) matching contribution $14,645; total $59,514; and Carolyn M. Yu&#8212;medical insurance $49,372; 401(k)
    matching contribution $14,000; telephone $660; total $64,032. For fiscal year 2025, the corresponding amounts were: Mr. Gerber&#8212;medical
    insurance $42,170; 401(k) matching contribution $15,133; total $57,303; Mr. Neibert&#8212;medical insurance $42,453; 401(k) matching
    contribution $16,133; total $58,566; and Ms. Yu&#8212;medical insurance $40,187; 401(k) matching contribution $15,217; telephone
    $660; total $56,064. The Company&#8217;s 401(k) plan provides a 100% safe-harbor match on participant salary deferrals up to 4% of
    eligible compensation, subject to applicable IRS limits.</span></td></tr>
