<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><b>&#160;</b></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><b>Outstanding
Equity Awards at Fiscal Year-End</b></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><b>&#160;</b></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">As
of June 30, 2026, none of the Company&#8217;s named executive officers held any outstanding stock options. As of June 30, 2026, none
of the named executive officers held any outstanding equity awards.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><b>&#160;</b></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><b>Retirement
Benefits</b></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">The
Company maintains a tax-qualified defined contribution plan under Section 401(k) of the Internal Revenue Code in which the named executive
officers are eligible to participate on the same basis as other eligible employees. Under the Plan&#8217;s safe harbor matching contribution,
the Company provides a 100% matching contribution on participant salary deferrals up to 4% of eligible compensation, subject to applicable
IRS limits. Safe harbor matching contributions are fully vested when made. Company matching contributions made on behalf of the named
executive officers are included in the &#8220;All Other Compensation&#8221; column of the Summary Compensation Table. The Company does
not maintain any defined benefit pension plan, supplemental executive retirement plan or non-qualified deferred compensation plan for
its named executive officers.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><b>&#160;</b></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><b>Potential
Payments Upon Termination or Change in Control</b></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">The
Company has employment agreements with Carolyn M. Yu and David W. Neibert that provide for severance benefits upon certain involuntary
terminations of employment. If the employment of Ms. Yu or Mr. Neibert is involuntarily terminated for any reason other than gross misconduct,
the Company is required to pay the executive severance compensation equal to six months of salary, payable over the six-month period
following the termination date. No severance compensation is payable if the executive voluntarily resigns or is terminated for gross
misconduct.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Based
on the annual salary rates in effect as of June 30, 2026, the estimated severance payments that would have been payable upon a qualifying
termination as of that date were $212,500 for Ms. Yu and $234,000 for Mr. Neibert.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Subsequent
to June 30, 2026, the Company entered into addenda to the employment agreements of Ms. Yu and Mr. Neibert, effective August 17, 2026,
providing for certain separation benefits following a Change in Control. Under the addenda, following the closing of a Change in Control,
each executive generally will continue employment for 90 calendar days at the same Base Salary. Upon expiration of that 90-day period,
the executive will be entitled to a lump-sum separation payment equal to six months of the executive&#8217;s annualized cash salary rate,
excluding Company benefits. If, during the 90-day period following the closing of a Change in Control, the executive is terminated by
the Company for any or no reason or separates from the Company by consent, the executive will remain entitled to the separation payment.
Upon the closing of a Change in Control, the separation benefit under the applicable addendum supersedes and replaces the existing six-month
severance benefit, and there will be no duplication of severance benefits.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"></span></p>

<!-- Field: Page; Sequence: 21 -->
    <div style="border-bottom: Black 1pt solid; margin-bottom: 6pt"><table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: 10pt"><tr style="vertical-align: top; text-align: left"><td style="width: 100%">&#160;</td></tr></table></div>
    <div style="break-before: page; margin-top: 6pt; margin-bottom: 0pt"><p style="margin: 0pt">&#160;</p></div>
    <!-- Field: /Page -->

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Nicholas
D. Gerber does not have an employment agreement or other arrangement providing for severance payments upon termination of employment
or a change in control of the Company.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Except
as described above, the Company does not have any agreement or arrangement with its named executive officers providing for additional
payments or benefits upon resignation, termination of employment or a change in control of the Company.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><b>&#160;</b></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><b>Pay
Versus Performance</b></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><b>&#160;</b></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><b>Say-on-Pay
Vote.</b> At the Company&#8217;s 2024 annual meeting, held on November 8, 2024, stockholders approved, on an advisory basis<b>, </b>the
compensation of the Company&#8217;s named executive officers, with 33,945,395 votes for, 1,309 votes against and 5 abstentions. At the
same meeting, stockholders voted on the frequency of future advisory votes on executive compensation, with the majority of votes cast
in favor of holding such a vote every three years. In light of this result, the Board determined that the Company will hold an advisory
vote on executive compensation every three years. Accordingly, the next advisory vote on named executive officer compensation is expected
to occur at the 2027 annual meeting, consistent with Rule 14a-21(a).</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><b>&#160;</b></span></p>

<p id="xdx_982_eecd--Additional402vDisclosureTextBlock_c20250701__20260630_zOkusi0fEJEf" class="xdx_phnt_RGlzY2xvc3VyZSAtIFBheSB2cyBQZXJmb3JtYW5jZSBEaXNjbG9zdXJlAA__" style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="From2025-07-01to2026-06-30" escape="true" id="Fact000014" name="ecd:Additional402vDisclosureTextBlock"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">The
Company is a smaller reporting company for the fiscal year ended June 30, 2026. Pursuant to Item 402(v) of Regulation S-K, the following
table and disclosure presents the most recent three years of Pay versus Performance information.</span></ix:nonNumeric></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

